# 15. DATABASE DESIGN

Create a complete PostgreSQL schema.

Save it as:

supabase/schema.sql

Include the following tables.

## profiles

Fields:
- id: UUID primary key referencing auth.users.id.
- full_name: TEXT.
- email: TEXT.
- programme: TEXT.
- role: TEXT with a default of student.
- created_at: TIMESTAMPTZ.

There must be no student_id column.

## courses

Fields:
- id: UUID primary key.
- course_code: TEXT.
- course_name: TEXT.
- department: TEXT, nullable.
- created_at: TIMESTAMPTZ.

## resources

Fields:
- id: UUID primary key.
- title: TEXT.
- description: TEXT.
- resource_type: TEXT.
- course_id: UUID referencing courses.id.
- file_path: TEXT.
- uploaded_by: UUID referencing profiles.id.
- examination_year: INTEGER, nullable.
- status: TEXT.
- rejection_reason: TEXT, nullable.
- created_at: TIMESTAMPTZ.
- updated_at: TIMESTAMPTZ.

## announcements

Fields:
- id: UUID primary key.
- title: TEXT.
- message: TEXT.
- image_path: TEXT, nullable.
- author_id: UUID referencing profiles.id.
- status: TEXT.
- published_at: TIMESTAMPTZ, nullable.
- created_at: TIMESTAMPTZ.
- updated_at: TIMESTAMPTZ.

## notifications

Fields:
- id: UUID primary key.
- title: TEXT.
- message: TEXT.
- category: TEXT.
- created_by: UUID referencing profiles.id, nullable where appropriate.
- created_at: TIMESTAMPTZ.
- scheduled_at: TIMESTAMPTZ, nullable.
- sent_at: TIMESTAMPTZ, nullable.
- status: TEXT.

## notification_recipients

Fields:
- id: UUID primary key.
- notification_id: UUID referencing notifications.id.
- user_id: UUID referencing profiles.id.
- is_read: BOOLEAN with a default of false.
- read_at: TIMESTAMPTZ, nullable.
- delivery_status: TEXT, where applicable.
- created_at: TIMESTAMPTZ.

## resource_reports

Fields:
- id: UUID primary key.
- resource_id: UUID referencing resources.id.
- reporter_id: UUID referencing profiles.id.
- reason: TEXT.
- description: TEXT, nullable.
- status: TEXT.
- reviewed_by: UUID referencing profiles.id, nullable.
- created_at: TIMESTAMPTZ.

## activity_logs

Fields:
- id: UUID primary key.
- actor_id: UUID referencing profiles.id, nullable.
- action: TEXT.
- entity_type: TEXT.
- entity_id: UUID, nullable.
- details: JSONB, where appropriate.
- created_at: TIMESTAMPTZ.

Add suitable indexes, foreign keys, unique constraints, timestamps, and validation constraints.

Use appropriate database functions and triggers for profile creation and auditing where necessary.

Prevent duplicate notifications to the same recipient when inappropriate.

Use transactions or carefully designed backend functions for operations that require multiple database changes to succeed together.

