# 16. BACKEND SECURITY AND ACCESS CONTROL

Security is a core requirement.

Enable Row Level Security on all relevant tables.

Implement policies ensuring that:

- Students can access only permitted resources.
- Only approved resources appear in public student listings.
- Authenticated users can submit permitted uploads.
- Users can edit or delete only resources they own, subject to moderation rules.
- Students can view and edit only their own profiles.
- Users can view only notifications intended for them.
- Students can mark only their own notifications as read.
- Only authorized administrators can publish announcements.
- Only authorized developers can perform privileged administrative actions.
- Students cannot assign themselves administrator or developer roles.
- Students cannot send notifications to other users.
- Students cannot modify activity logs.
- Storage permissions match the intended access rules.

Use trusted backend authorization for administrative operations.

Do not rely only on hiding buttons in the interface.

Do not expose:
- Supabase service-role keys.
- Database passwords.
- Private signing keys.
- Privileged notification credentials.
- Administrative secrets.

Use public client credentials only where appropriate, and enforce security on the backend.

For privileged account operations, use authenticated server-side functions with role verification.

Create a secure initial procedure for assigning the first developer administrator.

Never create a publicly accessible endpoint that grants administrator access to anyone.

